CYBRA MODULE 14 — WATCHDOG / SYSTEM HEALTH CONTROLLER
PATCH_ID=CYBRA-M14-PATCH-0001

1. The watchdog verifies system health; it does not create business truth.
2. A valid heartbeat is required.
3. Heartbeat age MUST NOT exceed HEARTBEAT_MAX_AGE_SECONDS.
4. Critical process health MUST be available.
5. Redis health MUST be verified when Redis is configured as required.
6. Backend A health MUST be independently verified.
7. Backend B health MUST be independently verified.
8. Backend A health MUST NOT substitute for Backend B health.
9. Backend B health MUST NOT substitute for Backend A health.
10. State freshness MUST be verified.
11. Stale state means FALSE/RETRY.
12. Missing health evidence means WAITING/BLOCKED.
13. Watchdog failure MUST NOT be converted into TRUE.
14. Watchdog failure MUST NOT authorize escrow release.
15. Watchdog failure MUST NOT authorize final release.
16. Watchdog failure MUST NOT authorize LIVE.
17. Watchdog MUST NOT sign a transaction.
18. Watchdog MUST NOT create a MetaMask signature.
19. Watchdog MUST NOT manufacture backend evidence.
20. Watchdog MUST NOT manufacture delivery evidence.
21. Watchdog MUST NOT manufacture buyer receipt evidence.
22. Watchdog MUST NOT establish GLOBAL_TRUE_100 by itself.
23. Watchdog PASS is only one required condition of the complete CYBRA state.
24. A successful watchdog check does not prove the business transaction itself.
25. TEST health evidence MUST NOT automatically become LIVE evidence.
26. Any correction MUST create a new PATCH_ID.
27. Frozen snapshots MUST NOT be silently modified.
28. Real transactions remain disabled in this controller.
